primary 
;High-resolution structures of HIV-1 reverse transcriptase/TMC278 complexes: Strategic flexibility explains potency against resistance mutations.
;
Proc.Natl.Acad.Sci.Usa 105 1466 1471 2008 PNASA6 US 0027-8424 0040 ? 18230722 10.1073/pnas.0711209105   
1       
;Crystal structures of clinically relevant Lys103Asn/Tyr181Cys double mutant HIV-1 reverse transcriptase in complexes with ATP and non-nucleoside inhibitor HBY 097.
;
J.Mol.Biol.            365 77   89   2007 JMOBAK UK 0022-2836 0070 ? 17056061 10.1016/j.jmb.2006.08.097 
2       
;Roles of conformational and positional adaptability in structure-based design of TMC125-R165335 (etravirine) and related non-nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitors that are highly potent and effective against wild-type and drug-resistant HIV-1 variants.
;
J.Med.Chem.            47  2550 2560 2004 JMCMAR US 0022-2623 0151 ? 15115397 10.1021/jm030558s         
3       
;Crystal structures of 8-Cl and 9-Cl TIBO complexed with wild-type HIV-1 RT and 8-Cl TIBO complexed with the Tyr181Cys HIV-1 RT drug-resistant mutant.
;
J.Mol.Biol.            264 1085 1100 1996 JMOBAK UK 0022-2836 0070 ? 9000632  10.1006/jmbi.1996.0698    
4       'The Lys103Asn mutation of HIV-1 RT: a novel mechanism of drug resistance.' J.Mol.Biol.            309 437  445  2001 
JMOBAK UK 0022-2836 0070 ? 11371163 10.1006/jmbi.2001.4648    
